# Everything under backtests/ is disposable scratch — CSV exports, caches, and
# study reports (backtests/study_output/) — and gets deleted periodically. The
# study CODE that used to need a gitignore exemption here now lives in
# scripts/backtest_study/, which is tracked normally.
backtests/*
!backtests/__init__.py
# docs/ is now GENERATED OUTPUT ONLY — the study map and the study-chart pages.
# The hand-written prose that used to live here is ARCHITECTURE.md at the repo
# root. Rebuild the whole folder with `make study-docs`.
docs/
.cache/
*_secret_*
*-key.json
audit/
portfolio/input/
portfolio/output/
# /journal/ is the LIVE TRADE RECORD and is never committed — not the raw broker
# pulls (they carry account identifiers), not trades.csv (real position sizes
# and P&L), not the reports (the same content in prose). The directory is
# created at runtime, so a fresh checkout simply has no journal until the first
# `make journal`. The Sheets TradeJournal tab, whose sharing the operator
# controls, is the only copy that leaves this machine.
#
# LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING. A bare `journal/` matches a directory of that
# name at ANY depth, which silently excludes `scripts/journal/` — the pipeline's
# own source code — from version control. Anchor it to the repo root.
/journal/